<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hywel Dda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 880–950</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Hywel the Good</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hywel Dda, Hywel the Good, was a Welsh king, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodri-the-great">Rhodri the Great</a>. He inherited Seisyllwg, united it with Dyfed around 920 to form Deheubarth and later ruled most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. He kept peace with the English king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan">Athelstan</a>, and Welsh tradition credits him with codifying the native laws of Wales.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hywel-dda.jpg" alt="Hywel Dda" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Humphrey Llwyd, David Powell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hyweldda_historieofcambria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
